export SOURCE_RECONCILIATION:
    precedence:
        For the same task and metric, an agent-reported value takes
        precedence over a conflicting harness value. This includes
        task status; an agent reporting completion wins over a harness
        reporting that the task is running.
    missingValues:
        Harness data can supply metrics not known by the agent. A
        report's unknown value is not a conflicting observed value.
        If neither source supplies a usable value, display unknown.
    freshness:
        Track live reporter health separately from task metric freshness.
        Mark live reporting stale after three missed heartbeats by default,
        corresponding to 30 seconds at the default 10-second interval.
        Mark live metrics stale when their last-checked time exceeds the
        configured threshold even if heartbeats continue. Retain stale
        values with their last-checked times. A heartbeat or harness update
        must not make unchecked agent metrics appear fresh. Staleness does
        not itself reverse agent precedence or imply failure or completion.
        Completed tasks retain valid final results without further heartbeats;
        reporter disconnection does not make those final results stale.
    attemptsAndOrdering:
        Each retry has a distinct attempt identity. Keep reports from prior
        attempts associated with those attempts; they cannot overwrite the
        current attempt. Within an attempt, apply only reports with sequence
        numbers greater than the last accepted number from that reporting
        source. Ignore older and duplicate reports without applying their
        status, metric values, or usage increments again. Preserve the
        established precedence between agent and harness sources.

export DATA_RELIABILITY_ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA:
    - A task-only harness remains visible with unsupported metrics unknown.
    - Agents use the same reporting contract and update without user prompting.
    - Agent completion overrides a harness reporting the same task as running.
    - Known harness usage can fill an agent's unknown usage metric.
    - A missing usage value is never rendered as zero usage.
    - Three missed default heartbeats mark live reporting stale.
    - Heartbeats alone do not refresh task metrics older than 30 seconds.
    - Completed task results remain valid without continuing heartbeats.
    - A delayed completion from an earlier attempt cannot complete a newer attempt.
    - Duplicate and out-of-order reports cannot roll back status or repeat usage.
    - Stale values remain visible with their last-update time.

export STALE_WORK_SWEEP:
    A periodic sweep finds dead or stuck work instead of waiting for a
    viewer to notice. It closes, with a final report, any task or build
    reported running whose agent or executor is gone, and it surfaces work
    that has been silent past a threshold for a human or orchestrator to
    judge.

export RELIABILITY_OPEN_QUESTIONS:
    - How will malformed reports and sequence continuity across reporter restarts be handled?
